    "narrative": "The June 1st slate presents a challenging landscape for LawDog, anchored by **Will Smith** as our premier start with a score of 61.54. **Will Smith** draws a favorable matchup against Rodriguez, whose 4.53 xERA provides the highest ceiling on our board today. While our infield is forced into a series of marginal starts, **Tyler Freeman** (53.61) narrowly edges out the rest of the unit. **Tyler Freeman** benefits from his position in the two-hole and, despite facing a league-average arm in Soriano, retains enough efficiency to clear the 50-point threshold, though we are keeping a watchful eye on his SB potential given the restrictive nature of his matchup.\n\nThe bench remains crowded with high-floor veterans who failed to clear our 40-point \"Zebras\" threshold, most notably **Luis Arraez** (38.34). While **Luis Arraez** is a perennial AVG anchor, the combination of a tough lefty in Drohan and his inability to contribute to our scarcity-driven SB category made him an easy exclusion today. Similarly, **Matt Chapman** (37.89) fell victim to the same left-handed SP skill penalty, leaving him relegated to the pine alongside **Masyn Winn** (37.64), who suffered from the unfortunate reality of facing a high-caliber arm like deGrom. \n\nRisks today are concentrated in the corners of our infield. **Jonathan Aranda** (47.17) is currently navigating a brutal matchup against Madden (2.31 xERA); while his dynamic platoon advantage provides a slight lift, his production is heavily dependent on his favorable order slot to mitigate the SP skill penalty. **Geraldo Perdomo** (45.20) rounds out the active roster, but with an SP skill penalty of -19% against Sheehan, he serves primarily as a stabilizer rather than a catalyst. We are prioritizing strict adherence to the 40-point floor to preserve our game caps, favoring the moderate stability of **Tyler Freeman** over the bench-bound **Jung Hoo Lee** and others who lack the projected volume to justify a start today.",
